Seed appearance and experimental settings from the runtime

A freshly provisioned workspace could not declare how its Orca looks or which
features are on: every browser opening the tile started at stock defaults, and
the same toggles got re-clicked after every workspace create.

The web client keeps settings in localStorage, and of the 213 top-level
`GlobalSettings` keys at `v1.4.190` it pulls exactly five from the runtime -
`theme` and the `experimental*` flags are not among them, so writing the
runtime's store changed nothing. A shared allowlist of appearance and capability
keys is now returned by `settings.get` and adopted exactly once, on a browser's
first visit, when localStorage holds no settings blob; nothing is written back
and nothing is re-imposed later, so these are defaults rather than policy.
Per-device ergonomics and credentials are excluded. A load that never reached
the store does not spend the first visit, so a browser whose first open happened
offline still seeds on the next one.

The store is the active Orca profile's `orca-data.json`
(`<userData>/profiles/<profileId>/orca-data.json`), not a per-workspace file;
under the AppImage's `orca serve` userData is `~/.config/orca`.

To test, set a seeded key in that `orca-data.json` and open the tile in a
browser with no Orca localStorage; then change it in the UI and reload to
confirm the workspace does not override the user. Covered by
`runtime-seeded-settings.test.ts` for the key picker,
`runtime-seeded-client-settings.test.ts` for the `settings.get` projection and
`web-preload-settings-seeding.test.ts` for the load path.
